          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Indian Companies Rush to Buy Cyber Insurance as AI Agent Risks and Rogue Chatbots Create New Liabilities",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Indian companies are increasingly purchasing cyber insurance policies to protect against AI-specific risks, including AI agents acting autonomously in harmful ways and chatbots providing incorrect or dangerous information. Insurers are redesigning their underwriting models to assess AI exposure, marking a significant shift in how corporate India manages technological liability. The global AI insurance market is projected for substantial growth, and India's uptake signals that boardrooms are treating AI risk as a mainstream financial concern rather than a fringe scenario.",
            "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/artificial-intelligence/increasing-ai-risks-boost-demand-for-cyber-insurance/articleshow/131047379.cms",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
